{"name":"Marsh Grass","hex":"#82763d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"marsh grass","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any coarse grass growing in marshes of genus Spartina.","Any wetland grass of genus Hymenachne."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marsh_grass"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hymenachne","blocks":[{"text":"Hymenachne, synonym Dallwatsonia, is a genus of widespread wetland plants in the grass family Poaceae. They are commonly known as marsh grasses. They are distributed in tropical and subtropical regions of Asia, the Americas, and the Pacific Islands. A species from the Americas, H. amplexicaulis, is well known in other parts of the world as an introduced and invasive species."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Hymenachne_amplexicaulis_1584.jpg/330px-Hymenachne_amplexicaulis_1584.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hymenachne","wikidata":"Q2198236"},{"title":"Marsh","blocks":[{"text":"In ecology, a marsh is a wetland that is dominated by herbaceous plants rather than by woody plants. More in general, the word can be used for any low-lying and seasonally waterlogged terrain. In Europe and in agricultural literature, low-lying meadows that require draining and embanked polderlands are also referred to as marshes or marshland."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Meadowlands_Lyndhurst.jpg/330px-Meadowlands_Lyndhurst.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marsh","wikidata":"Q30198"},{"title":"Grass","blocks":[{"text":"Grass refers to various families of plants. The three major families of grasslike plants are true grasses (Poaceae), sedges (Cyperaceae), and rushes (Juncaceae). Lawns and pasturelands are typically composed of true grasses, five of which cover 46% of the world's arable land: rice, wheat, maize, barley, and sugar cane."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Poa_annua.jpg/330px-Poa_annua.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grass","wikidata":"Q643352"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Coastal_marsh_profile.png/500px-Coastal_marsh_profile.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Coastal_marsh_profile.png/500px-Coastal_marsh_profile.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Marsh in shallow water on a lakeshore","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACoastal_marsh_profile.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Water_Lily_-_geograph.org.uk_-_483063.jpg/500px-Water_Lily_-_geograph.org.uk_-_483063.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Water_Lily_-_geograph.org.uk_-_483063.jpg/500px-Water_Lily_-_geograph.org.uk_-_483063.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"White water lilies are a typical marsh plant in European areas of deeper water.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWater_Lily_-_geograph.org.uk_-_483063.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Xanthocephalus_xanthocephalus_-100_Mile_House%2C_British_Columbia%2C_Canada_-male-8.jpg/500px-Xanthocephalus_xanthocephalus_-100_Mile_House%2C_British_Columbia%2C_Canada_-male-8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Xanthocephalus_xanthocephalus_-100_Mile_House%2C_British_Columbia%2C_Canada_-male-8.jpg/500px-Xanthocephalus_xanthocephalus_-100_Mile_House%2C_British_Columbia%2C_Canada_-male-8.jpg?utm_so